From 9af00095f3dde01c6f53124685b47c10bf32d67f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hangxiang Ma <hangxiang.ma@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 05:46:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 110/144] dt-bindings: phy: qcom,x1e80100-csi2-phy: Add SM8750
 CSI2 PHY

The SM8750 camera subsystem exposes six CSI2 D-PHY blocks that follow the
same programming model as Kaanapali. Describe the SM8750 CSI2 PHY using a
"qcom,sm8750-csi2-phy" compatible with the "qcom,kaanapali-csi2-phy"
fallback, so the CAMSS binding can instantiate the CSIPHY nodes as
separate phy devices.

Signed-off-by: Hangxiang Ma <hangxiang.ma@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260721-add-support-for-camss-on-sm8750-v6-1-a5f841061d18@oss.qualcomm.com

Import-Patch: pkgs/linux-kernel/sm8750/dodge/patches/7.3/0142-dt-bindings-phy-qcom-x1e80100-csi2-phy-Add-SM8750-CS.patch
Import-SHA256: ab33f0a6fa5ed12eb4fd25e746d2fbb3bc511fec3cab20ebf3eb2d9e7ff61a2c
Import-Provenance: mail headers
(cherry picked from commit c512561129d5d479064954a74667eb05d9561ce2)
